      "reason": "医者 (いしゃ) is the standard and natural term for a medical doctor (physician) in Japanese, which is the most common meaning of 'doctor' in general daily life. 博士 (はかせ) refers to a person holding a doctorate (PhD) or an expert, not a medical professional."
